1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,900
TIMES HE STARTED OVER: 47

2
00:00:01,100 --> 00:00:03,300
47 times, Leo started over.

3
00:00:01,150 --> 00:00:02,200
47 RESTARTS

4
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:04,900
Every time, the same voice stopped him.

5
00:00:05,800 --> 00:00:07,600
Start Monday.

6
00:00:07,700 --> 00:00:09,900
You know my voice too.

7
00:00:10,150 --> 00:00:13,400
It took him 47 restarts to learn

8
00:00:10,950 --> 00:00:13,400
what disciplined people never say out loud.

9
00:00:13,700 --> 00:00:15,800
One year earlier.

10
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:19,100
Five more minutes.

11
00:00:16,100 --> 00:00:18,900
RESTART #1 · THE ALARM

12
00:00:19,900 --> 00:00:22,300
The plan lasted exactly one alarm.

13
00:00:22,700 --> 00:00:24,400
Exam on Friday. He just had to start.

14
00:00:23,800 --> 00:00:28,500
Watch one more first.

15
00:00:24,100 --> 00:00:27,100
RESTART #6 · THE RESEARCH

16
00:00:29,400 --> 00:00:31,300
Four hours of advice. Zero pages read.

17
00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:33,100
Tuesday. He'd already missed Monday.

18
00:00:32,900 --> 00:00:36,500
Week's ruined. Start Monday.

19
00:00:33,100 --> 00:00:36,100
RESTART #14 · THE MISSED MONDAY

20
00:00:35,100 --> 00:00:37,300
One missed day became a missed week.

21
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:41,300
You earned this.

22
00:00:38,100 --> 00:00:40,400
RESTART #23 · THE REWARD

23
00:00:40,900 --> 00:00:42,400
One "reward" undid five days.

24
00:00:42,900 --> 00:00:44,800
It's not good enough.

25
00:00:43,100 --> 00:00:44,800
RESTART #35 · THE DRAFT

26
00:00:45,300 --> 00:00:46,400
Nobody ever heard it.

27
00:00:46,800 --> 00:00:49,300
Plan it perfectly first.

28
00:00:50,100 --> 00:00:51,500
RESTART #47 · THE PERFECT PLAN

29
00:00:50,100 --> 00:00:51,500
Sound familiar?

30
00:00:54,400 --> 00:00:57,800
You're just not built for this.

31
00:00:58,300 --> 00:01:01,300
He'd never talk to a friend like this.

32
00:01:02,100 --> 00:01:04,300
Only to himself.

33
00:01:04,900 --> 00:01:08,100
6:02 AM. He couldn't sleep.

34
00:01:09,100 --> 00:01:12,300
Then he saw Maya. She never misses a run.

35
00:01:13,900 --> 00:01:15,400
She had one too.

36
00:01:15,300 --> 00:01:17,500
Stay in bed.

37
00:01:19,300 --> 00:01:22,100
And she went anyway.

38
00:01:23,800 --> 00:01:26,100
You hear it too?

39
00:01:26,200 --> 00:01:28,100
Every morning.

40
00:01:28,200 --> 00:01:30,500
Then how do you still go?

41
00:01:30,600 --> 00:01:33,400
I stopped asking it.

42
00:01:32,500 --> 00:01:34,500
DAYS MAYA FELT LIKE RUNNING: 9 / 212

43
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:46,400
Disciplined people don't feel like it either.

44
00:01:37,100 --> 00:01:46,400
Not Maya. Not athletes. Not anyone.

45
00:01:40,100 --> 00:01:46,400
They just stopped asking.

46
00:01:49,200 --> 00:01:51,500
Just start Monday.

47
00:01:51,700 --> 00:01:53,900
5... 4... 3... 2... 1.

48
00:01:54,100 --> 00:01:56,500
1. Don't ask. Count 5 to 1. The feeling never votes yes.

49
00:01:54,700 --> 00:01:56,500
This time, he didn't answer it.

50
00:01:56,700 --> 00:02:00,000
2. Make it stupid small. One push-up. One page.

51
00:02:00,100 --> 00:02:03,500
3. Never miss twice. Missing once is life. Missing twice is a new habit.

52
00:02:03,550 --> 00:02:04,450
Pointless.

53
00:02:03,600 --> 00:02:05,500
DAY 1

54
00:02:05,050 --> 00:02:05,950
You're tired.

55
00:02:06,550 --> 00:02:07,450
It's raining.

56
00:02:08,050 --> 00:02:08,950
Check your phone.

57
00:02:09,550 --> 00:02:10,450
Everyone's staring.

58
00:02:11,100 --> 00:02:13,900
Day 9: sick. Day 10: one push-up anyway.

59
00:02:11,850 --> 00:02:12,750
Missed one. Quit.

60
00:02:12,350 --> 00:02:13,000
TIMES HE STARTED OVER: 48?

61
00:02:14,050 --> 00:02:14,950
Too hard.

62
00:02:15,550 --> 00:02:16,450
Order pizza.

63
00:02:17,050 --> 00:02:17,950
Not good enough.

64
00:02:18,550 --> 00:02:19,450
Skip today.

65
00:02:20,050 --> 00:02:20,950
Tomorrow.

66
00:02:22,350 --> 00:02:23,250
Just today...

67
00:02:24,650 --> 00:02:25,550
later?

68
00:02:26,900 --> 00:02:26,500
DAY 180

69
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:30,700
180 days. Not one of them felt easy.

70
00:02:31,300 --> 00:02:34,500
Same wall. Same hand. Different man.

71
00:02:36,500 --> 00:02:37,300
DAY 181

72
00:02:37,400 --> 00:02:41,400
He never needed another Day 1.

73
00:02:42,200 --> 00:02:44,500
Months later. A new face at the bar.

74
00:02:42,900 --> 00:02:47,300
Everyone's watching.

75
00:02:47,700 --> 00:02:50,300
Just do one. That's it.

76
00:02:52,900 --> 00:02:55,700
Now it was his turn to say it.

77
00:02:56,400 --> 00:02:59,700
The voice never fully goes away.

78
00:03:00,100 --> 00:03:03,700
He just stopped asking it for permission.

79
00:03:04,050 --> 00:03:10,800
DISCIPLINE

80
00:03:05,700 --> 00:03:10,800
Motivation asks how you feel.

81
00:03:06,500 --> 00:03:10,800
Discipline doesn't ask.

82
00:03:07,500 --> 00:03:10,800
What's the line your villain always says? Comment it.

83
00:03:11,200 --> 00:03:14,700
TIMES HE STARTED OVER: 47

